+# Feature Specification: Bulk import
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Implemented
+**Input**: "Add `importTasks(list, text)`: one task per line as `title;priority;tags`; returns `{ imported, rejected }`."
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: Each non-blank line is `title;priority;tags`; priority and tags may be empty or omitted (normal, none).
+- **FR-002**: Tags are separated by whitespace.
+- **FR-003**: Blank lines are skipped; `line` numbers count from 1 over all lines, blanks included.
+- **FR-004**: Valid lines are added through `list.add`; any line it refuses (bad title, priority or tag, duplicate title, also within the text) is rejected as `{ line, reason }` with the error message; other lines still import.
+- **FR-005**: A line with more than three `;`-separated parts is rejected.
+- **FR-006**: Exported from `src/index.ts`; `\n`, `\r\n` line endings accepted.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Titles cannot contain `;`. Priorities are case-sensitive (`high`), as in `add`.
